
"smart_sources:2026-07-27 - Bipartisan Bill Would Improve Congress’s Broken Budget Process.md": {"path":"2026-07-27 - Bipartisan Bill Would Improve Congress’s Broken Budget Process.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1vfmh5r","at":1785795033967},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785347162654,"size":9672,"at":1785795034036,"hash":"1vfmh5r"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,10],"#":[11,32],"####Creating a Bipartisan Commission to Reduce the Deficit":[33,44],"####Creating a Bipartisan Commission to Reduce the Deficit#{1}":[35,44],"####Additional Budget Transparency and Accountability Reforms":[45,46],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:":[47,63],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:#{1}":[49,49],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:#{2}":[50,50],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:#{3}":[51,51],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:#{4}":[52,52],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:#{5}":[53,54],"####The bill includes several additional provisions intended to improve fiscal transparency, congressional oversight, and coordination:#{6}":[55,63]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Dhiraj Thapa","target":"Dhiraj Thapa","line":5},{"title":"Demian Brady","target":"Demian Brady","line":6},{"title":"H.R. 9452","target":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/9452/text?s=1&r=3&hl=%22H.R.+9452%22","line":13},{"title":"S. 2765","target":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/senate-bill/2765","line":21},{"title":"first bipartisan budget-reform package","target":"https://www.ntu.org/publications/detail/broken-budget-blues-senators-enzi-whitehouse-may-have-a-remedy-for-that","line":21},{"title":"looming insolvency","target":"https://www.ntu.org/foundation/detail/social-security-and-medicare-trust-fund-depletion-dates-move-closer","line":27},{"title":"H.R. 3289","target":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3289?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22HR+3289%22%7D&s=1&r=1","line":37},{"title":"S. 4012","target":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/4012","line":37}],"metadata":{"title":"Bipartisan Bill Would Improve Congress’s Broken Budget Process","source":"https://www.ntu.org/foundation/detail/bipartisan-bill-would-improve-congresss-broken-budget-process","author":["[[Dhiraj Thapa]]","[[Demian Brady]]"],"published":"2026-07-27","created":"2026-07-29","description":"The congressional budgeting process is badly broken. Lawmakers routinely miss statutory deadlines, rely on continuing resolutions, and generally complete their appropriations work only after the fiscal year has begun. These recurring failures have weakened fiscal discipline and contributed to a national debt approaching $40 trillion.  Representatives Steve Womack (R-AR), Ed Case (D-HI), Bill Huizenga (R-MI), and Scott Peters (D-CA) recently introduced the Budgeting for a Better America Act (BBAA, Author(s): Dhiraj Thapa, Demian Brady"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},